From 375821b8c98784a63b93ab66b43389a7e58b2db3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marks-jhojan <153632015+marks-jhojan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] runtime: UNDS_LED, UNDS_TRIGGER and physical trigger
 travel in pad events

Three switches for a companion that drives the DualSense directly
(adaptive triggers and light bar through DSX now, through SDL later):

  UNDS_LED=0              scePadSetLightBar / ResetLightBar no longer reach
                          SDL_SetGamepadLED; the "led" event is still
                          published. Two writers of the DualSense output
                          report (SDL in the port and the companion's
                          driver) would otherwise overwrite each other's
                          light bar colour.
  UNDS_TRIGGER=<l2>,<r2>  press threshold of L2 / R2 on the 0-255 travel
                          (default 30,30, the value sample_host() had
                          hard-coded). The port gives the game 0 or 255
                          for a trigger, so this is where the shot
                          happens; with an adaptive "weapon" effect it
                          can be moved to the point where the trigger
                          breaks.
  pad l2a r2a             physical L2/R2 travel of the host sample (before
                          the threshold), same deadband and 8 ms limit as
                          the sticks: lets the companion calibrate effect
                          zones against the threshold.

All three work with or without UNDS_EVENTS; with none of them set the
runtime behaves as before and prints nothing. hello gains led and trig.
Protocol stays 1 (fields only added); UNDS_VERSION 0.3.0.

